# XSH 2.12 Status Information
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# What a parent can learn about a child. Most of the section is tested
# with wait(), waitid() and _Exit(); the .cov file points there. These
# two cover what they do not.

assertion  XSH.2.12-status-information.001
anchor     functions/V2_chap02.html#2.12
class      required
says       A child that stops itself, is continued and then exits with status
           5, before its parent has waited for any of that, leaves one status
           only: after waitid(WEXITED|WNOWAIT) reports the exit, waitpid()
           with WUNTRACED|WCONTINUED reports the exit with status 5 (not the
           stop or the continuation), and a second waitpid() fails with
           ECHILD.
note       The stop and the continuation status are replaced by the new one.
           WCONTINUED is XSI: without XSI the test uses WUNTRACED alone.
timeout    30
test       t/001-new-status-replaces.c

assertion  XSH.2.12-status-information.002
anchor     functions/V2_chap02.html#2.12
class      required
says       With two threads blocked in waitpid() and a third in
           waitid(WEXITED|WNOWAIT), all for the only child, when the child
           exits at least one of the three obtains its status, and not both
           of the two waitpid() threads do.
note       Which threads obtain it is unspecified. Threads left blocked at
           the end are cancelled; the test counts only returns seen
           within 3 s of the exit.
timeout    30
test       t/002-wait-threads-wnowait.c
